ioned are  there other consequences that could come  out of this if none of this happens  well it's a good question i think that  what you're having is a lot of public  outcry about the president  in terms of legal consequences it's an  open question of course  what his exposure is at this point but  you do have lots of people within the  white house  heading for the exits now we've already  had two cabinet members resign  potentially more on the way  and lots of folks who work in the white  house and more broadly in the republican  party are saying  well we had our four years here let's  move on it's time to move on now  you talk about moving on what about the  republican party this has become the  party of trump  how does it go forward at this point  well it's trying to figure that out  right now and there are pretty big  schisms you have someone like lisa  murkowski who i mentioned earlier who is  now  openly questioning her own future within  the party but at the same time just this  week the republican national committee  itself  met in florida and reelected unanimously  ronald mcdaniel  who is the head of the republican party  and a top ally of the president and you  also had a majority of house republicans  actually after the riots vote to object  to the certification of the electoral  college so those folks are still  standing with president trump  it's going to be a massive crisis in the  party that's going to play out for quite  some time  yeah so much to discuss gabe thank you  for the insight we appreciate it
 

